<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Plagiarismresearchintegrity Policy - AJSMR</title><style>body{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0;background:#f5f6f8;color:#222;line-height:1.65}.container{max-width:1050px;margin:35px auto;padding:0 20px}.card{background:#fff;border-radius:8px;padding:32px;box-shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.08)}h1{margin-top:0;color:#222;font-size:30px}h2{font-size:21px;margin-top:28px;color:#333}li{margin:8px 0}.note{background:#f0f4f8;padding:14px 16px;border-left:4px solid #555;margin:20px 0}.small{font-size:13px;color:#666}</style></head><body><div class="container"><div class="card"><h1>Plagiarism, Research Integrity & Retraction Policy</h1><div class="note">AJSMR expects authors, editors and reviewers to protect the integrity of the scholarly record.</div><h2>Plagiarism</h2><p>Plagiarism includes presenting another person's words, ideas, data, figures or intellectual contributions as one's own without appropriate attribution. Close paraphrasing and unattributed reuse are also concerns.</p><h2>Duplicate and Redundant Publication</h2><p>Authors should not submit or publish substantially overlapping work as separate publications without transparent justification and disclosure.</p><h2>Fabrication and Falsification</h2><p>Fabrication of data or results, falsification or inappropriate manipulation of research materials, images or analyses are serious research-integrity concerns.</p><h2>Authorship</h2><p>All listed authors should have made an appropriate contribution and should approve the submitted version. Authorship changes require appropriate explanation and consent.</p><h2>Image and Data Integrity</h2><p>Images and data should be presented accurately. Where manipulation is suspected, the journal may request original data or files.</p><h2>Investigation</h2><p>Credible concerns may lead to requests for clarification, supporting information, consultation with editors or communication with an author's institution where appropriate.</p><h2>Corrections and Retractions</h2><p>Published articles may be corrected, issued an expression of concern, or retracted when evidence demonstrates that the scholarly record requires such action. Notices should clearly identify the affected article and reason.</p><h2>Ethical Framework</h2><p>AJSMR follows recognized publication-ethics principles, including applicable COPE guidance, while retaining responsibility for applying procedures appropriate to the journal.</p><p class="small">AJSMR local testing version. Final wording should be confirmed against actual journal practices before live publication.</p></div></div></body></html>